&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Deprecate+and+Remove%5C%3A+document.requestStorageAccessFor%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Re: Intent to Deprecate and Remove: document.requestStorageAccessFor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Rick+Byers%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Rick Byers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260728" rel="nofollow"&gt;Tue, 28 Jul 2026 14:29:07 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;LGTM1, thanks Johann!

I appreciate that there's some risk here (0.018% is still a lot of
pageloads). But given the context of an optional feature not well supported
across browsers and useful only for the small fraction of Chromium browser
users with 3PCs disabled, I believe the risk is low and also trust that you
and your team will respond to any incidents effectively.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

On Mon, Jul 27, 2026 at 5:50 PM Johann Hofmann &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="adc7c2c5ccc3c3838383edcac2c2cac1c883cec2c0"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:

&gt; Hello!
&gt;
&gt; I'm happy to report that rSAFor usage has been driven down significantly. 
&gt; Given
&gt; that the previous LGTMs were for deprecation only, *I'm seeking** final
&gt; approval to remove document.requestStorageAccessFor in M153*.
&gt;
&gt; After the biggest consumer of the API removed usage in June, we are now
&gt; at 0.018% of pageloads
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/4332"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/4332&lt;/a&gt;&gt;. To
&gt; address Mike's earlier concern, usage of navigator.permissions.query for
&gt; top-level-storage-access has been driven down massively as well, to &lt;=
&gt; 0.03% of pageloads (this is an upper bound as I am naively assuming at most
&gt; one query per pageload, which is the best I can do with the available
&gt; metrics).
&gt;
&gt; From brief spot testing of the few larger sites still using the API, the
&gt; only noticeable loss of functionality is the lack of automatic (silent)
&gt; login between their related sites. This is an expected result (and only
&gt; happens if the user actually blocks 3PCs).
&gt;
&gt; As such, I'd like to proceed and remove the API now. We'll use a feature
&gt; flag (StorageAccessAPIRelatedWebsiteSets) to have an emergency lever for
&gt; unexpected breakage, and plan to actually remove the code in the M154/M155
&gt;  timeframe.
&gt;
&gt; Please let me know if you have any questions!
&gt;
&gt; Thanks,
&gt;
&gt; Johann
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; On Mon, Nov 24, 2025 at 5:03 PM Johann Hofmann &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="bad0d5d2dbd4d4949494faddd5d5ddd6df94d9d5d7"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; Thank you everyone! Just wanted to ack the concerns again and will try to
&gt;&gt; report back on any bumps along the way.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Sun, Nov 23, 2025 at 4:50 PM Rick Byers &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="700212095e5e5e301318021f1d19051d5e1f0217"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; LGTM3 to deprecate.
&gt;&gt;&gt; Yes I'm quite sure that worst case we can no-op this. I hope it doesn't
&gt;&gt;&gt; get stuck there though, total removal doesn't seem like it should be too
&gt;&gt;&gt; hard, but we still need to put the work in to do it responsibly.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Thanks!
&gt;&gt;&gt;   Rick
