On 7/29/26 4:27 p.m., Rick Byers wrote:
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;blockquote style="border-left: #5555EE solid 0.2em; margin: 0em; padding-left: 0.85em"&gt;&lt;tt&gt;We discussed this in API owners today and Alex made a compelling 
&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;argument for why there is no need to namespace-scope IWA APIs (they're 
&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;already heavily scoped by the fact they exist only in the niche IWA 
&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;operating environment). Alex, Reilly, Edman and I then met to discuss 
&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;the tradeoffs further and agreed that we'd remove the namespace 
&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;scoping (eg. window.setShape).
&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;pre style="margin: 0em;"&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;tt&gt;Given this significant change, I suggest we reset the lgtm counter. 
&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;I'm LGTM1 with this new plan (once the spec is updated to reflect it).
&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;pre style="margin: 0em;"&gt;

Thanks,
   Rick


