&lt;pre&gt;Hi Alex and Rick,

Thanks for taking a look at this.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

We actually shipped the version of &lt;usermedia&gt; that is closest to and
aligned with the specifications. However, we are maintaining the current OT
as a &quot;reverse OT.&quot; This means that if a site keeps the OT token present,
the &lt;usermedia&gt; element will retain its legacy behavior (more context on
this approach here:
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/google.com/g/origin-trials-core/c/HXPxsWc1Ez4/m/7F77s0PRAwAJ"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/google.com/g/origin-trials-core/c/HXPxsWc1Ez4/m/7F77s0PRAwAJ&lt;/a&gt;
)

Currently, we have two partners using &lt;usermedia&gt; who need more time to
transition, so we would like to extend this &quot;reverse OT&quot; for the next 3
milestones.

On Wed, Jul 22, 2026 at 5:24 PM Rick Byers &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="483a2a31666666082b203a2725213d2566273a2f"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:

&gt; In particular, I appreciate the (temporary) requirement &quot;To ensure our
&gt; partners currently using the Origin Trial do not experience unexpected
&gt; service disruptions&quot;. But what if we decouple the question of extending the
&gt; OT (for the &quot;legacy API&quot;) from the question of just shipping the current
&gt; API? Is there some reason the current API does not meet our bar for I2S? If
&gt; we can ship it, I'd also be supportive of extending an OT to give your
&gt; customers a bit more time (3 more months) to migrate to the shipped API.
&gt;
&gt; Rick
&gt;
&gt; On Wed, Jul 22, 2026 at 11:21 AM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="94e7f8fdf3fce0f8edbababad4f7fce6fbf9fde1f9bafbe6f3"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt; wrote:
&gt;
