&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/524"&gt;https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/524&lt;/a&gt;. A comment on that thread
indicates a real website that needs it:
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/524#issuecomment-314870317"&gt;https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/524#issuecomment-314870317&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

I think it's about different cache invalidation for reloads vs not, under
the heuristic that the user wants to reset things when reloading.

